{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-2982",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a={b}^{x}$ is equivalent to ${log}_{b}⁡a=x$\n\nIf we compare ${2}^{x}=64$ with $a={b}^{x},$ we get $a=64$ and $b=2.$\n\nTherefore, the equation ${2}^{x}=64$ is equivalent to ${log}_{2}⁡64=x.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
